Usage: agent-deck feedback
       agent-deck feedback bug|idea [flags]   (report a problem; see 'agent-deck feedback bug --help')
       agent-deck feedback bug --from-agent --title T --what W [--json]   (agent sessions: no prompt, gh only)
       agent-deck feedback mine [--json]       (the reports filed from this machine and their state)
       agent-deck feedback fixed N --fixed|--not-fixed [--comment C]   (answer "Is it fixed for you?")
       agent-deck feedback agent-consent [--off]   (let agent sessions post with --from-agent; asks y/N)
       agent-deck whats-new [--json]           (what changed since you last looked; your fixed reports first)

Rate agent-deck and optionally leave a comment.

How it works:
  1. You are asked for a rating (1-5, n to never ask again, q to quit).
  2. On a valid rating you may add a short comment.
  3. BEFORE anything is sent, the CLI shows a disclosure block with:
       - the public URL (https://github.com/asheshgoplani/agent-deck/discussions/600),
       - that it posts via the `gh` CLI under your GitHub account,
       - your GitHub username (as seen by `gh api user -q .login`),
       - the exact body that will be posted.
  4. You confirm with `y`. Default is N — pressing Enter declines.

Failure mode:
  If `gh` fails (not installed, not authenticated, network error), the
  CLI prints an error and exits non-zero. There is NO silent clipboard
  or browser fallback on this path — nothing is sent without consent.

A private/anonymous feedback channel is being designed for a future
release — track in https://github.com/asheshgoplani/agent-deck/issues/679.

Prompt frequency (v1.7.41+):
  The TUI auto-prompt appears after 7 launches or 3 days of use,
  whichever comes later. If you dismiss it, we wait 14 days before
  asking again. Maximum 3 prompts per version. Pressing `n` at any
  step is a permanent opt-out. `agent-deck feedback` always works
  on demand regardless of pacing.
